{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "כטומאת", :translit "k'tum'at", :gloss "like the impurity of"} {:he "כטומאת נדתה", :translit "k'tum'at nidatah", :gloss "like the impurity of her menstruation"} {:he "כטומאת הנדה היתה", :translit "k'tum'at ha-nidah hayetah", :gloss "like the impurity of the menstruating woman she was"} {:he "וזרקתי עליכם מים", :translit "v'zarakti aleichem mayim", :gloss "and I will sprinkle upon you water"} {:he "השוכן אתם בתוך טומאותם", :translit "ha-shochein itam b'toch tuma'otam", :gloss "who dwells with them amidst their impurities"} {:he "זבה זובו זובה", :translit "zavah zovo zavah", :gloss "discharge her discharge his discharge her"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 11, :occurrences ["זבה" "זובו" "זובה"]}], :frame {:text "A menstruant (נדה) attains purification through water, as Numbers 19 describes the ashes of the red heifer mixed with spring water for purifying those impure from contact with the dead. Ezekiel 36:25 similarly promises: וזרקתי עליכם מים טהורים וטהרתם. A kohen is permitted to be in the same house as a menstruant, but Leviticus 21:11 forbids a kohen from contracting corpse impurity, so he may not enter under the same roof as a corpse. The eleven-day interval between menstruation and the next is delineated in Mishnah Niddah 10:1, which counts the eleven days between two menstrual periods as the days of zivah.", :sources ["Numbers 19:17-19" "Ezekiel 36:25" "Leviticus 21:11" "Mishnah Niddah 10:1"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 11, :occurrences ["זבה" "זובו" "זובה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "זבה", :refs ["Leviticus 15:19"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "זובו", :refs ["Leviticus 15:2" "Leviticus 15:3" "Leviticus 15:33"], :n 3, :lens :exact} {:phrase "זובה", :refs ["Leviticus 15:26"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:23:39.035196919Z", :model "glm-5.2"}